 "archDir": "docs/architecture",
 "notes": [
  "ids follow the rules of acme-shop.answer.json (same contract, same notes). What is new here is in the lines below.",
  "every route of routes/api.php gets the /api prefix the framework adds, so it is INFERRED; a Route::prefix('v1')->group(...) adds /v1 inside it; routes/web.php adds nothing, so its route is EXTRACTED. file/line stay at the Route:: call; the five routes of Route::apiResource('orders', ...) share the line of that call (needle 'orders'), carry attrs.action (index store show update destroy) and the parameter is the singular {order}. `update` is PUT (Laravel also answers PATCH; one fact is expected).",
  "screens: a Flutter screen is a widget class named in a GoRoute (route = its path); the line is the class declaration; the id uses the folder of the app (apps/customer -> customer). price_tag.dart is a widget but not a screen. A Blade view is a screen with route = widget = the view name (receipt), line 1 (the screen sits on the whole file); the id uses the folder of the workspace (backend).",
  "functions: the id is fn:<file>#<Class>.<name>; a top-level Dart function has no class; the up/down of an anonymous migration class (return new class extends Migration) have no class either (fn:<file>#up). Only named things are facts: an unnamed Dart constructor (const HomeScreen({super.key})), a closure, a fn () => arrow and function (Blueprint $table) {...} are not. exported: Dart = neither the name nor the class starts with _ ; PHP = public (private function summary is false). endLine = the line of the closing brace (an arrow with => ends on its own line). async = Dart async.",
  "Dart has no export of a declaration and PHP has none either: there is no export fact in acme-delivery. A relation sits on the method that returns it (public function items()), with cardinality 1-n on both sides like Prisma's 1-n pair. A Dart import is checked only when it is package:acme_customer/... or ./ ../ relative.",
  "job:mail/SendReceipt is the consumer (the class that implements ShouldQueue); its refs are the producers, the places that call SendReceipt::dispatch(...). queue:mail sits on the onQueue('mail') call. No env name is in two files on purpose.",
  "extraFacts: the five PHP `use App\\...` imports (file to file by composer.json autoload.psr-4 \"App\\\\\" -> backend/app/). They are expected facts like the others and must be found by the extractors; they live apart ONLY because the sanity test of B1-T1 (test/foundation-fixtures.test.mjs, resolvesTo) knows only ./ ../ and package:<name>/. Whoever owns that test must teach it psr-4; then these move into facts. Until then the measure (B1-T18) and the join (B1-T14) must read facts + extraFacts.",
  "coverage is { num, den } (acme-shop rules): a fact is cited when a backtick span of docs/architecture holds its route path (the method does not count), its screen route or its table name as a whole word. Here GET and POST /api/v1/orders are both cited by the path. The unowned root file (.gitignore) is expected: only a path with a \"/\" in \"Where in the code\" can own a file."
 ],
